WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We should go visit the shrine together

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:39.060
I won a vacation to the beach for two in the shopping district raffle!

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.320
I'll invite Yuzu-san to the beach!

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.750
Going to the beach with Yuzu-san!

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:46.180
Oh, no, no.

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:48.040
Yuzu-san, yaa-hoi!

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.070
I said all that, but I'm not sure how to invite her.

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:54.630
Should I be nonchalant and cool?

00:01:54.630 --> 00:01:59.080
No, cheap tricks can backfire if executed
poorly. I should just be straightfor—

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.400
Oh, Gonta-san!

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.300
Welcome! What's the matter?

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:05.770
Y-Yuzu-san, u-um...

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.080
The weather's very nice today.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:08.820
Yes.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:18.070
A trip with the two of us by ourselves would be too awkward.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:22.060
It'd be better to invite Mayu as well and make it three.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:28.520
But, this coupon is only for two
people; one of us will have to pay.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.440
There's no way Mayu will pay, so it looks like I'll have to.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.270
Oh well, it's unavoidable.
I guess I can buy my own ticket.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.780
Is that a beach house coupon?

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:40.760
Yoshino?!

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:44.510
Going to the beach sounds great!

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.300
Actually, I think inviting Yoshino
would be less trouble than Mayu.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.420
Perfect timing Yoshino, how would you like to go the beach with Yuzu-san and someone else?

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:58.220
That sounds great! Are you sure it's all right to give Mayu-sama, Yuzu-san, and me such a wonderful gift?

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.320
Why would it be you three?
Why am I not included?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.580
You're going to the beach with Mayu? I'll go too!

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:07.090
If Mayu-sama is going, I shall accompany you.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:08.800
This will be a lively trip!

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.510
There's nothing like going
to the beach during summer.

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.290
Yes.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.170
Exactly.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.100
Oh, everyone's here.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.670
It seems I didn't bring enough tea.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:19.220
Oh, Yuzu, want to go to the beach with all of us?

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:22.150
Sure, it'll be fun with so many people!

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:25.380
I did it!

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:32.660
The pure blue skies!

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.540
The white-sandy beach!

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.460
All the different colored swimsuits!

00:03:37.460 --> 00:03:40.410
Yuzu-san looks absolutely beautiful in her swimsuit!

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:39.670
Gonta-san!

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:49.080
That's how it should've been.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:52.210
I should've seen her perfect swimsuit.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:56.030
I should've seen her once in a lifetime swimsuit.

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:57.080
Stop repeating yourself! That's annoying!

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:59.040
You know...

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.320
This inn is actually pretty nice.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:04.120
It's a bit old, but it has a sort of vintage feel as well.

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:08.390
I would have preferred it to be more like a resort.

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:09.750
Let's go to our room.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.740
I think this is it.

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.900
Shamo-chan!

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.220
You're all here. What's going on?

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:24.440
Shamo-chan, why are <i>you</i> here?

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:29.330
Are this big storm and my misfortune both your fault?!

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.570
They are not. I won a vacation to the
beach in the shopping district raffle.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.020
Why is the Goddess of Poverty winning a lottery?!

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.580
This is our room though.

00:04:39.580 --> 00:04:41.950
My room has a leak.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.040
I'm sorry to hear that.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.270
You should just stay here with us then.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:50.240
This room looks fine; one more person shouldn't hurt.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:53.500
The more the merrier!

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:57.160
Gonta, you can take the leaky room.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.050
That's right! Gonta-san is a boy after all.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:04.230
You'd better get going, Gonta.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:12.060
Yukina-sensei, are you starting to see it?

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:16.310
It's no good! I feel like I'm trying to squeeze out a dry rag.

00:05:16.730 --> 00:05:19.290
Nothing is coming out.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:24.330
I thought I'd come up with good ideas if
I locked myself up in a beachside inn.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:26.780
Anyhow, you need to make time for the actual drawing.

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.800
The manuscript won't get done in time
if the storyboard isn't finished today.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.180
I know!

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.220
She's struggling this time.

00:05:34.220 --> 00:05:38.410
We don't have anything to do if there's no storyboard.

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.590
We just have to stand here and wait.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.380
What's the matter?

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:43.290
Reporting in!

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:45.910
The Yaoyorozu-dou people are in the Octopus Pot Room!

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.150
What?!

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.080
Chief!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.270
I hope this doesn't interrupt her progress.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:59.070
Damn it! This weather is thwarting my plans!

00:05:59.070 --> 00:06:02.340
Well, I really don't mind.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.620
I didn't want get a tan anyway.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.220
Plus, you're paying for the entire trip.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:10.320
You all tagged along on your own!
I'm not paying for your travel expenses!

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.630
Oh, really? If keep acting so stingy,
your precious Yuzu will hate you!

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.230
Yeah Gonta, even when it's raining
there are other ways to have fun.

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:20.170
You brought it?

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:23.140
Playing games on vacation has its own merit.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.580
There's no external input/output port!

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:27.890
How old is this television?!

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:33.590
Calm down Mayu-sama, we're on a trip; the games can wait.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.650
Yeah, a hot spring bath usually comes first!

00:06:37.100 --> 00:06:38.600
Hot spring?

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.560
Right, I still have a chance.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.590
This hot water is great!

00:06:47.590 --> 00:06:49.940
Yuzu-san, I'll wash your back.

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:52.000
Oh, thank you very much.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:53.690
You won't wash mine?

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.550
I'll wash your back, Mayu!

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:57.820
No, I will!

00:06:57.820 --> 00:06:59.000
What did you say?!

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.500
Mayu's silky-smooth skin is mine!

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:02.500
President, you have nice, smooth skin.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:06.710
Oh no, it's yours that has the smooth texture.

00:07:08.980 --> 00:07:11.150
Do you feel itchy anywhere?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:14.520
Let's see... a little more to the right...

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.080
I will!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.880
Shampoo me too!

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.880
Make sure you wash thoroughly.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.770
Oh, I will.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.340
I'm done!

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.380
I haven't been to a hot spring in years!

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:29.250
If business continues to thrive, we'll go have a wild
time at a luxury resort instead of this dilapidated inn.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:36.790
Of course...

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:42.540
Which would you prefer?

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:49.680
A cold bottle of coffee milk right after a bath is the best!

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:51.990
Click.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.440
This is heaven.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:08:00.580
Oh, this an old arcade cabinet!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:02.700
This is why I shouldn't look down on old inns.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.940
Here it goes, Yuzu-sama!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:06.940
Sure!

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:09.530
There!

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:15.250
Here... it goes!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:24.210
Yuzu, go easy on her.

00:08:24.210 --> 00:08:26.290
Sorry, it's been a while since I last played.

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:33.800
Well, this is quite different from the schedule, but Yuzu-san seems to be enjoying herself.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.800
This might actually be a good thing!

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:44.140
Now that I think about it, this trip
is for two nights and three days.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:47.730
It raining one day isn't that big of a deal.

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:49.780
Oh, Gonta, didn't you know?

00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:50.610
Know what?

00:08:50.610 --> 00:08:53.360
Unfortunately, it'll keep raining for a long
while, even after tomorrow and the next day.

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:54.860
You're kidding!

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:57.560
Why would I kid?

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:58.200
Look.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:01.120
Next up is weekly forecast for each region.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:03.910
It's slated to rain in all regions.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:06.170
This weekend will have a monster storm.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:06.500
See?

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:10.990
I-Impossible! That's nonsense!

00:09:10.990 --> 00:09:14.390
Humans' weather forecasts are never dependable to begin with.

00:09:14.390 --> 00:09:17.290
I'll check with the rain god for this region right now.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:19.130
You're an idiot.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:22.650
Humans' forecasts these days are quite accurate.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:26.500
Also, you shouldn't be asking the rain god anyway.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:28.690
Look at the news closely.

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:32.520
A typhoon is approaching right now.

00:09:32.520 --> 00:09:35.240
That's a hurricane god.

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:42.080
Perfect, number sixteen grew big and strong this year!

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.510
This time we'll cut across the archipelago!

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:46.700
Let's go!

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:49.030
It's over.

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:51.730
It's all over.

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:52.970
Everything.

00:09:52.970 --> 00:09:55.140
Well, we can't help that.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:57.800
I'm a little disappointed this is happening on our vacation though.

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:02.980
Yeah, I bought brand new swimsuits for this trip.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:05.190
New swimsuits?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:17.310
If it's for your new swimsuits, Yuzu-san, I'll do something about this typhoon; it's no big deal.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:20.690
Yuzu-san, please watch me.

00:10:20.690 --> 00:10:25.820
I will smash a typhoon or two if you wish!

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:27.760
I'll do anything for love!

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:34.340
No one would have trouble if every issue could be resolved with things like love and friendship!

00:10:34.580 --> 00:10:36.820
Well, you're going up against a typhoon.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:42.470
Ugh, if the train system shuts down because of this and I can't return to Tokyo...

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:45.050
I won't be able to take the prep school's mock exam!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.970
That's what you get for coming to the
beach when you should be studying.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.850
What's that?! Why can't I come to the beach?

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:56.850
I can't feel the summer shine on my skin?

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:03.360
Are you saying I should stay in the dank library
study hall and memorize English for the exam?!

00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:05.810
Please, stop fighting you two.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.730
Oh, it's the angel, Nana.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:11.690
There's still hope. Look at this!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:15.370
A floating tea stalk!

00:11:11.690 --> 00:11:15.370
TL Note: A symbol of good luck.

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:20.050
This is no good!

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.710
This kind of plot won't do!

00:11:22.710 --> 00:11:29.500
I should begin with Karin and Nana forming a team to turn away the typhoon using the power of friendship!

00:11:30.130 --> 00:11:36.310
The two will build a super robot, that draws in power from an even greater typhoon, to fend it off.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:38.280
That's the same thing.

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:44.070
Wait, maybe what they thought to be a typhoon was actually the monster, Hectopascal!

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:47.030
A ridiculous storyline like that won't work.

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:51.440
I'll go buy some snacks from the lobby.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.910
I'm sure you'll think of something good after eating some sweets.

00:11:55.870 --> 00:12:00.210
We should do what we can to help as well.

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:01.790
Chief, what are we going to do?

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:04.760
You'll see.

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:09.210
Wait Yuzu, you'll catch a cold if you go outside dressed like that!

00:12:12.530 --> 00:12:15.310
I know! I'll just double their bad luck.

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:18.990
On top of the typhoon hitting, a black cat will walk in front of them,

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:25.820
their sandal strap will snap, and to finish it all off, they'll lose a set of stamps that's almost full!

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:29.570
That storyline even scares <i>me</i>.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:33.030
Chief, what good is us cleaning doing?

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:39.080
Cleaning the room will help to clear her head and brainstorm better. It's quite useful.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:46.470
But, even if I want to take on a typhoon or two, how do I actually smash them?

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:51.070
Realistically, the power of love can't change a typhoon's path.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.760
Time keeps passing while I keep thinking.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.690
I have to come up with something quickly!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:03.730
What is this?

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.750
I have to stop this typhoon no matter what!

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:11.530
I have an idea. First, prepare a big barrel.

00:13:11.530 --> 00:13:15.360
Then fill that barrel with sardines.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:18.400
Get as much salt as you can...

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:19.070
What is this?

00:13:19.530 --> 00:13:26.060
Is someone trying to teach me how to
stop a typhoon easily using manga?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.800
This method is worth trying!

00:13:37.800 --> 00:13:38.930
Barrel!

00:13:42.610 --> 00:13:43.940
Sardines!

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:48.190
Salt.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:54.200
Now what do I do with these?

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.670
Pickle the sardines with the salt inside
the barrel and make nam pla.

00:13:59.550 --> 00:14:00.450
Nam pla?

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.710
It's a must-have condiment for Thai food!

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:09.400
After you make the nam pla, sprinkle it on different dishes to get...

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:12.370
That's not how you stop a typhoon.

00:14:12.370 --> 00:14:14.140
That's how you eat Thai style.

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:16.010
Thai style.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:18.620
Boring.

00:14:29.790 --> 00:14:31.840
The storm's become quite violent.

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:36.020
That aside, Meiko, are you prepared?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:40.470
Of course! I hope you don't regret this later.

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:44.980
The winner obtains the right sleep in
a futon next to Mayu-sama tonight.

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:46.980
Very well.

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:48.480
It's a showdown!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:51.750
Receive my serve if you can!

00:14:51.750 --> 00:14:54.390
Stop your babbling and bring it on!

00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:59.790
That's nothing!

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:04.390
Not yet!

00:15:06.890 --> 00:15:09.800
Why don't you just sleep with her in the middle?

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:13.480
Look at this, President.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:16.750
If you invert this ball point pen, the yukata on the woman becomes a swimsuit!

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:18.070
Yeah, let's buy that.

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:21.370
Are those souvenirs?

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:23.290
Yeah, for my master.

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:26.330
How about this? This is a standard souvenir.

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.570
Well, that's a little...

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.160
Here's something pretty awesome.

00:15:31.160 --> 00:15:35.820
A 32-colored ball point pen!
It's as heavy as a boneless ham!

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:37.980
I don't need it.

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:39.850
I guess some people might not like it.

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:42.610
I think snacks would be the best.

00:15:42.610 --> 00:15:45.820
Here's this week's souvenir snack!

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.320
Barnacle Acorn Buns!

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:50.580
Look, it's filled up on the inside of the lid too!

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:52.150
Akane, you're here too?

00:15:52.150 --> 00:15:54.050
Shamo-chan, I see you're here with some friends as well.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:55.100
Look, it's filled.

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:56.410
Um...

00:15:56.410 --> 00:16:00.510
I'm Shinozaki Akane, chief editor for Yukina-sensei.

00:16:00.510 --> 00:16:02.290
Yukina's here too?

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:05.780
Yes, she's staying here because
she's stuck on her manuscript.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:10.130
Well maybe we should all go visit her to cheer her up.

00:16:11.140 --> 00:16:14.650
This is hopeless. Is there any other way?

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:16.910
Again?

00:16:17.310 --> 00:16:20.320
Is there any other way to stop the typhoon?!

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:26.340
There's only one way, but it's much too
dangerous and should only be a last resort.

00:16:26.830 --> 00:16:28.330
What does it entail?

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.850
First, prepare a tire and a rope.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:32.090
Then...

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:42.770
I did it! The training was successful!

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.100
I'm under the 10 percent line!

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:50.850
Isn't that how you lower your body fat percentage?

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:53.040
That's not even a pun anymore.

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:56.500
She's in a slump.

00:16:56.500 --> 00:16:59.370
How about taking a short rest?

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:02.330
Let's have dinner together in our room!

00:17:02.980 --> 00:17:06.820
This is no good. There's just no
way I can stop the typhoon!

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.290
Again?

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:13.230
Because of the wave, my swimsuit...

00:17:22.130 --> 00:17:25.040
This is it.

00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:28.560
What's wrong, Gonta? Aren't you going to eat?

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.420
I need to go right now.

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:31.850
I have to go.

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:33.560
I <i>have  to stop it.</i>

00:17:34.010 --> 00:17:36.310
Nip slips. Slips!

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:38.310
Slips?

00:17:45.890 --> 00:17:48.870
Let's dig in right now!

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.890
Thanks for the food!

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:54.940
I'll definitely stop it.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.250
This crab is good!

00:18:01.250 --> 00:18:02.820
The abalone too!

00:18:05.720 --> 00:18:08.450
For Yuzu-san's smile!

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:12.120
This clam is huge!

00:18:12.120 --> 00:18:16.550
Mayu-sama, don't eat just tuna; have some vegetables as well.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:18.550
But I like tuna!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.480
For Yuzu-san's new swimsuit.

00:18:25.690 --> 00:18:28.220
Gonta's plate is all that's left.

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:30.160
It'd be a waste, so why don't we eat it?

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.980
I want beer!

00:18:35.730 --> 00:18:37.020
And most of all...

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.510
for nip slips!

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:45.850
Yukina-sensei, you're not even done with
the storyboard yet, so you can't have beer!

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.110
Just a little bit should be fine.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:51.660
It might even help me think of something quicker.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:54.620
Being a manga artist is definitely a lot of work.

00:18:54.620 --> 00:19:00.480
Why don't we all pitch ideas for Yukina's manga?

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:02.370
That's a good idea!

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:06.760
If the plot is stagnant, why not introduce a new character to help carry the series?

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:09.020
Maybe a love rival, Daikichi-kun!

00:19:09.110 --> 00:19:15.230
How about making it three brothers? Daikichi, Chuukichi, Shoukichi, who are all rivals! Isn't that good?

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:19.510
How about a murder incident revolving Daikyou-chan?

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:24.990
Isolated in a seaside holiday house due to a storm, they leave cryptic messages and die one by one.

00:19:24.990 --> 00:19:26.940
The person you're waiting for won't come.

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.700
The wish won't be granted.

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:30.370
You'll lose very few items.

00:19:30.530 --> 00:19:34.750
Oh, I know those! They're called dying messages, right?

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:41.600
Speaking of which, it's not really a "dying message", but
Gonta-san still hasn't come back after that cryptic speech.

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:43.120
That's not really cryptic.

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:45.590
It's actually easy to understand.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:49.970
Could he have gone to face the hurricane god alone?

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:57.480
This typhoon is nothing!

00:20:03.710 --> 00:20:05.730
Did a fly hit me just now?

00:20:07.560 --> 00:20:16.370
Here at Cape Haniwa, a strong wind, clocking in at over 50 mph, has been blowing since morning and a typhoon warning has now been issued.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:23.170
Did Gonta die?

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:29.920
As you can see, the typhoon number sixteen is
continuing to move north while remaining strong.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:31.040
Wait a second.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:33.700
Did she just say number sixteen?

00:20:33.700 --> 00:20:37.120
That's right, typhoon number sixteen is headed this way.

00:20:37.120 --> 00:20:38.420
Let me use your phone.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:42.480
Hello?

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:44.070
Hello?

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:47.800
Oh, Mayu-chan, it's been a while! What's up?

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.870
Oh, it's about that online game?

00:20:49.870 --> 00:20:53.830
I've been busy with work lately.
Sorry I can't play with you.

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:56.920
What? A time-sensitive quest?!

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.490
Limited rare materials?!

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:00.710
No way! It's only good for today?!

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:06.840
It turned away!

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:10.510
I knew she was in charge of number sixteen.

00:21:22.090 --> 00:21:24.850
Yukino, don't you have to finish the manuscript?

00:21:24.850 --> 00:21:27.940
Thanks to you guys, I completed a good storyboard.

00:21:27.940 --> 00:21:34.360
At any rate, I feel sorry for Gonta-san. He was really looking forward to swimming, but he caught cold.

00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.470
He's one unlucky guy.

00:21:36.960 --> 00:21:38.020
Thank you!

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:40.690
Slip...

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.750
Oh, Yuzu, yours slipped too.

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:54.570
Slip.

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:55.810
It slipped?

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.290
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:20.350
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.460
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:31.780
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:38.250
So stay here forever

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:43.490
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.400
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize that small memory that won't disappear is the key. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.370
Next Episode

00:23:27.620 --> 00:23:29.820
I see there are a lot of gods who love games!

00:23:29.820 --> 00:23:32.560
Even in Takamagahara, I was pretty badass at playing games...

00:23:32.560 --> 00:23:36.460
Mayu-sama, bragging about being badass rates high on the boring stories survey.

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:38.950
Oh, that's right! Can I have some Barnacle Acorn Buns?

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.370
Recollection Antiquities

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:41.500
That's a souvenir for my master.
